# 5. Time and Space Complexity

This is another very important viva topic.

### Time Complexity

\[
\boxed{O(n \times W)}
\]

Where:
- n = Number of items.
- W = Maximum knapsack capacity.

**Why?**

We create a DP table containing (n+1) rows and (W+1) columns.

We visit every cell exactly once and perform a constant-time calculation.

Therefore:

\[
O(n \times W)
\]

### Space Complexity

\[
\boxed{O(n \times W)}
\]

Because we store the entire 2D DP table.

### Complexity summary

| Operation | Complexity |
|---|---|
| Creating DP table | O(nW) |
| Filling DP table | O(nW) |
| Finding selected items | O(n) |
| Overall Time | O(nW) |
| Space | O(nW) |

